# check that if we receive mail with a nice envelope sender and a
# no-bounce from field, we mix the two to create a less broken from
# field.
depends empty-inbox
protocol lmtp submit
receive 1
220 LMTP imapscript.test.oryx.com
send 1
LHLO localhost
receive 10
250-imapscript.test.oryx.com
250-BURL IMAP IMAP://imapscript.test.oryx.com
250-ENHANCEDSTATUSCODES
250-BINARYMIME
250-PIPELINING
250-8BITMIME
250-CHUNKING
250-SMTPUTF8
250-STARTTLS
250 DSN
send 1
mail from:<whatever@test.oryx.com> x-oryx-id=1 x-oryx-time=1181649536
receive 1
250 2.1.0 Accepted message from whatever@test.oryx.com
send 1
rcpt to:<script@test.oryx.com>
receive 1
250 2.1.5 Will send to script@test.oryx.com
send 1
data
receive 1
354 Go ahead (1 local recipients)
send 7
From: "Do Not Reply" <>
To: script@test.oryx.com
Date: Wed, 7 Sep 2005 16:53:18 -0000
Message-ID: <41432431243242314234231432432431242343243243432423143241234231423@test.oryx.com>

Woo!
.
receive 1
250 2.1.5 script@test.oryx.com: OK
use main
send 1
a noop
receive 4
* 1 EXISTS
* 1 RECENT
* OK [UIDNEXT 2] next uid
a OK done
send 1
b fetch 1 body.peek[header.fields (from)]
receive 5
* 1 FETCH (BODY[HEADER.FIELDS (From)] {32}
From: whatever@test.oryx.com

)
b OK done
end
